      {
        "id": "ai-video-generator",
        "tag": "genai",
        "tagLabel": "GenAI",
        "title": "🎬 AI video generator",
        "desc": "An end-to-end AI filmmaking pipeline that turns a topic or script into a fully-produced short video , AI-written story, consistent characters, narration, generated visuals, TTS voiceover, background music, and a rendered MP4, with a Streamlit UI and a Supabase-backed FastAPI service.",
        "detail": [
          "An end-to-end AI Filmmaking Assistant that turns a topic, a description, or a raw script into a fully-produced short video , an AI-written story, consistent characters, scene-by-scene narration, AI-generated visuals, AI voiceover, background music, and a rendered MP4 , with a Streamlit UI for authoring and a Supabase-backed FastAPI service for project/scene persistence and editing. {{img:architecture}}",
          "<strong>🏗️ Architecture:</strong> three cooperating parts , a FastAPI backend (<code>ai_video_generator/</code>) owning all AI generation logic (story, characters, narration, images, TTS, music, captions, rendering) and persisting projects/scenes to Supabase; a Streamlit multi-page frontend (<code>ai_video_gen_ui/</code>) for authoring, scene-by-scene editing, and a video gallery; and a root orchestrator (<code>main.py</code>) hosting both a newer Supabase-integrated pipeline and the legacy file-based pipeline that predates the Supabase migration. Deployed on Render as a Poetry-managed Python 3.11 service.",
          "<strong>✍️ Two story-creation flows:</strong> an <em>AI Filmmaker</em> flow (<code>/generateVisualScenes</code>) where the user supplies just a story description and the AI writes the full story, invents consistent characters, writes narration + image prompts per scene, sources images, generates TTS narration, and persists everything to Supabase; and a <em>Filmmaker</em> flow (<code>/generateVisualsFromScenes</code>) where the user supplies their own scene breakdown and the AI composes a cohesive story around it while preserving the exact scene count and descriptions. {{img:home}}",
          "<strong>📖 Story &amp; character generation:</strong> uses Google Gemini (<code>gemini-2.0-flash</code>) with a system prompt enforcing a hook, integrated visual description, and a clear beginning/middle/end arc driven by user-supplied tone/theme/age settings. Prompts are pulled live from Langfuse's prompt registry at runtime (with local fallback) so they can be iterated without a redeploy. Characters are generated as structured JSON (Pydantic schema , species, name, age, gender, outfit, hair) to keep every character's appearance consistent across every scene image. {{img:story-gen}}",
          "<strong>🎥 Narration, visuals, voice &amp; music:</strong> a structured-output narration/image-prompt generator writes a strict cinematic Image Prompt Framework (subject, action, expression, outfit, background, style, lighting, camera angle) per scene; images are sourced by building Pollinations.ai URLs at a fixed seed/model for style consistency and uploaded to Supabase Storage; narration audio comes from Pollinations' TTS with an automatic fallback to <code>edge-tts</code> if the primary call fails; background music is mixed under narration via MoviePy with fade in/out and volume ducking; and <code>whisper-timestamped</code> produces word-level timing for burning subtitles onto the final render. {{img:script-gen}}",
          "<strong>🎬 Rendering &amp; recovery:</strong> MoviePy sequences per-scene image + narration clips (narration-driven pacing, cross-fades), composites video and audio, and encodes with GPU-accelerated <code>h264_nvenc</code>. Dedicated recovery endpoints let a user re-download failed images, re-run just the render step, or patch a single scene's image/prompt without regenerating the whole project , backing a Streamlit <strong>Video Editor</strong> page for scene-by-scene review and regeneration. {{img:editor}}",
          "<strong>🗄️ Persistence &amp; observability:</strong> Supabase (Postgres + Storage) holds <code>projects</code> and <code>scenes</code> tables plus a <code>scenes-media</code> bucket for generated images/audio, accessed through a FastAPI project/scene CRUD API. Every generation stage is traced end-to-end with Langfuse (<code>@observe</code> spans for story → characters → narration → images → audio → video), giving full request/prompt visibility across the pipeline.",
          "<strong>🖥️ Streamlit frontend:</strong> a multi-page authoring app , a generation form (video/story/character settings), a story-only generator, a script-driven generator, a gallery of rendered videos, a scene-by-scene Video Editor (edit an image prompt, regenerate a preview, then commit it back into the project), and resume/error-recovery pages for continuing an interrupted run. {{img:gallery}} {{img:all-stories}}",
          "<strong>🛠️ Stack:</strong> FastAPI, Google Gemini (structured outputs via Pydantic), Pollinations.ai (image + audio), <code>edge-tts</code>, <code>whisper-timestamped</code>, MoviePy 2.x with NVENC encoding, NLTK, Supabase (Postgres + Storage), Langfuse (tracing + prompt registry), Streamlit, Poetry, and Render for deployment.",
          "<strong>🎞️ Sample output:</strong> a fully rendered sample story video (\"Blue Panther\") generated end-to-end by the pipeline , AI-written story, generated visuals, narration, and background music. {{vid:blue-panther}}",
          "<strong>📺 App walkthrough:</strong> a screen recording of the Streamlit UI , generation form, scene-by-scene editing, and the video gallery. {{vid:app-walkthrough}}"
          // ,"I later tried to build an actual product around this pipeline , see <a href=\"project.html?id=ai-film-making-assistant\">🎬 AI film-making assistant →</a>."
        ],
        "images": [
