      {
        "id": "face-recognition",
        "tag": "vision",
        "tagLabel": "Computer vision",
        "title": "🪪 Face recognition attendance system",
        "desc": "Bachelor's mini project: a Django attendance system that recognizes students live from webcam feeds, using OpenCV DNN face detection, OpenFace embeddings, and a custom-trained classifier , I led the team building it end-to-end.",
        "detail": [
          "My bachelor's mini project: an end-to-end Face Recognition Attendance System (FRAS) that automates classroom/faculty attendance using a computer-vision pipeline (face detection → face embedding → face classification) integrated into a full Django web application. I led the team building this end-to-end, from dataset creation and model training to the Django backend and live recognition pipeline. {{img:login}}",
          "<strong>🧠 System architecture:</strong> the system works in three stages.<ol style=\"margin:8px 0 0 20px; padding:0;\"><li>Dataset creation , capture and augment face images of each student, organized by Branch → Year → Section</li><li>Model training , detect faces, extract deep-learning face embeddings, and train a classifier to recognize each student</li><li>Live recognition & attendance marking , a faculty member opens a webcam feed in the Django app, the trained pipeline recognizes students in real time, marks them Present/Absent, saves the result as a CSV, and emails it to the faculty</li></ol>Pipeline: Webcam Frame → Face Detection (OpenCV DNN / SSD) → Face Embedding (OpenFace) → Classification (scikit-learn) → Attendance Record. {{img:activity-diagram}}",
          "<strong>📦 Dataset creation & augmentation:</strong> for each student, I captured a batch of face images directly from a live webcam feed and stored them in a dedicated per-student folder so the raw dataset stayed organized by identity from the start. Since a handful of webcam shots per person isn't enough to train a reliable classifier, I augmented that raw set , varying brightness, flipping images horizontally, and applying small rotations , to multiply the number of usable training samples per student and make the model more robust to real-world lighting and pose differences. The augmented images were then run through the face detector to crop and align just the face region, and each cropped face was passed through the embedding model to build the final feature dataset used for training. {{img:capturing}}",
          "<strong>🎯 Face recognition engine:</strong><ul style=\"margin:8px 0 0 20px; padding:0;\"><li>Face detection using OpenCV's deep-learning DNN face detector (Caffe SSD model: deploy.prototxt.txt + res10_300x300_ssd_iter_140000.caffemodel)</li><li>Face embedding extraction using the pretrained OpenFace Torch model (openface.nn4.small2.v1.t7), producing a 128-d feature vector per face</li><li>Face classification using a scikit-learn model trained on the extracted embeddings and serialized as machinelearning_face_person_identity.pkl</li><li>A unified pipeline_model() function chaining detection → embedding → classification, returning the annotated frame plus recognized identities</li><li>Real-time webcam recognition loop that aggregates recognized student IDs across frames until the operator presses Esc</li></ul> {{img:training}}",
          "<strong>🖥️ Django web application:</strong><ul style=\"margin:8px 0 0 20px; padding:0;\"><li>User authentication with login/logout, django-allauth integration, and a full password-reset flow</li><li>Student registration ('Add Student') , faculty register a new student with name, registration ID, branch (CSE/IT/CSM), year (1–4), section (A/B/C), and a profile picture used as face-training data</li><li>Faculty profile management with name, phone, email, and profile picture</li><li>Live attendance capture , opens the webcam, runs the ML recognition pipeline against the enrolled class, and automatically marks each student Present or Absent</li><li>Automatic CSV export of every attendance session, organized by date, branch, year, section, and period</li><li>Automatic email delivery of the generated CSV to the taking faculty via SMTP</li><li>Attendance search & filtering by branch/year/section/period/date using django-filter</li><li>Student record lookup and update pages</li></ul> {{img:take-attendance}}",
          "<strong>🗄️ Database design:</strong> three core models , Faculty (one-to-one with Django's User; name, phone, email, profile picture), Student (name, registration ID, branch, year, section, profile picture stored per branch/year/section), and Attendence (faculty name, student ID, auto date/time, branch, year, section, period, status defaulting to 'Absent'). {{img:class-diagram}}",
          "<strong>🛠️ Tech stack:</strong><ul style=\"margin:8px 0 0 20px; padding:0;\"><li>Django 3.0.5 for the web framework</li><li>django-allauth and Django's built-in auth for authentication</li><li>django-filter for attendance search/filtering</li><li>OpenCV (cv2) and its DNN module for face detection</li><li>OpenFace (Torch model via OpenCV DNN) for face embeddings</li><li>Caffe SSD (via OpenCV DNN) for the detector backbone</li><li>scikit-learn for the face classifier</li><li>NumPy for numerical computing</li><li>Gradio for a standalone demo UI</li><li>SQLite3 as the database</li></ul>"
        ],
        "images": [
          { "id": "login", "src": "media/images/Face_attendance_system/Login Page.png", "caption": "Login page" },
          { "id": "home", "src": "media/images/Face_attendance_system/Home Page.png", "caption": "Home page" },
          { "id": "add-student", "src": "media/images/Face_attendance_system/Add Student.png", "caption": "Add student form" },
          { "id": "student-added", "src": "media/images/Face_attendance_system/Student added Successful.png", "caption": "Student added successfully" },
          { "id": "capturing", "src": "media/images/Face_attendance_system/Capturing images.png", "caption": "Capturing face images for training" },
          { "id": "training", "src": "media/images/Face_attendance_system/Training the ML model.png", "caption": "Training the ML model" },
          { "id": "take-attendance", "src": "media/images/Face_attendance_system/Take Attendance.png", "caption": "Take attendance , live recognition" },
          { "id": "take-attendance-temp", "src": "media/images/Face_attendance_system/Take attendance temp.png", "caption": "Live recognition in progress" },
          { "id": "attendance-success", "src": "media/images/Face_attendance_system/Attendance Success.png", "caption": "Attendance marked successfully" },
          { "id": "search-attendance", "src": "media/images/Face_attendance_system/Search Attendance.png", "caption": "Search attendance" },
