      {
        "id": "medintelbot",
        "tag": "rag",
        "tagLabel": "Healthcare AI",
        "title": "🩺 MedIntelBot , A Local RAG-Powered Medical Assistant",
        "desc": "💡 A locally hosted RAG application delivering medical insights from real medical PDFs , no cloud-based LLM APIs. 🔧 Built with LangChain, FAISS, CTransformers, and Chainlit for speed, privacy, and precise document retrieval.",
        "detail": [
          "This project is a locally hosted RAG (Retrieval-Augmented Generation) application designed to provide medical insights using real medical PDFs – all without relying on cloud-based LLM APIs. {{img:hero}}",
          "💡 MedIntelBot leverages a custom fine-tuned stack to deliver document-grounded answers in real-time via a locally run LLM interface.",
          "🔧 Built using LangChain, FAISS, CTransformers, and Chainlit, this project is optimized for speed, local resource efficiency, and precise document retrieval.",
          "<strong>Key Highlights:</strong><ul style=\"margin:8px 0 0 20px; padding:0;\"><li>1️⃣ Local LLM Integration: 💠 Utilizes the LLaMA 2 7B model, running locally via CTransformers with quantized binaries, enabling full privacy and offline access. 💠 Avoids the need for any OpenAI or HuggingFace API calls , perfect for secure and local deployments.</li><li>2️⃣ Efficient Document Ingestion &amp; Chunking: 💠 Medical PDFs are automatically loaded and chunked. 💠 All documents are vectorized using all-MiniLM-L6-v2 embeddings and stored in-memory via FAISS, making retrieval fast and efficient.</li><li>3️⃣ Custom Retrieval Chain with Prompt Engineering: 💠 A tailored RetrievalQA chain is built with a zero-hallucination prompt that discourages guesses and restricts the answer to only retrieved context chunks.</li><li>4️⃣ Interactive Frontend via Chainlit: 💠 Seamless chat interface designed using Chainlit, offering a minimalistic but robust user experience for real-time question answering. 💠 Backend dynamically loads the LLM, embedding model, and vector store, wrapping everything into a session-persistent chatbot.</li></ul>",
          "This solution is highly adaptable for any domain where confidential document querying is required, and serves as a blueprint for local, privacy-first RAG systems.",
          "#GenerativeAI #LangChain #FAISS #LLama2 #Chainlit #AIApplications #RAG #Python #LLM"
        ],
        "images": [
          { "id": "hero", "src": "media/images/med_intel_bot.png", "caption": "MedIntelBot chat interface" }
        ],
        "link": [
          { "label": "View on GitHub →", "href": "https://github.com/Vishnu-add/MedIntelBot" }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "embedding-finetune",
        "tag": "rag",
        "tagLabel": "Retrieval",
        "title": "🧠 Fine-tuning Embedding Models for Domain-Specific Semantic Search",
        "desc": "💡 Working with general-purpose embedding models is great , until you hit the wall with domain-specific information retrieval. Fine-tuned BAAI/bge-small-en on a public-health knowledge base to push semantic search beyond generic understanding.",
        "detail": [
          "I tackled the challenge of enhancing semantic understanding when working on a specialized knowledge base (KB) for public health. Here's what made this journey technically exciting:",
          "🔗 <strong>Ensured Document-Query Consistency with Metadata Mapping:</strong> 💠 Before training anything, I built a strict document-page integrity checker across ~700+ KB entries and mapped them to 2500+ metadata-tagged FAQ queries. This validation loop avoided the classic trap of training on mismatched or noisy labels.",
          "🧱 <strong>Generated a Three-Part Training Architecture:</strong> 💠 A complete pipeline was constructed with: <code>queries</code> , unique, UUID-tagged questions; <code>relevant_docs</code> , precise mappings to document-page identifiers; <code>corpus</code> , cleaned and indexed knowledge base text.",
          "🧪 <strong>Smart Splitting with Custom Index Alignment:</strong> 💠 Custom <code>train_test_split</code> logic was applied, with index resetting to maintain referential integrity between all components , something often overlooked when using pandas with relational text data.",
          "🔧 <strong>Finetuning Using LlamaIndex + SentenceTransformers:</strong> 💠 Used <code>EmbeddingQAFinetuneDataset</code> from LlamaIndex after encountering structure-loading issues , solved by serializing and reloading from JSON. Fine-tuned a <strong>BAAI/bge-small-en</strong> model using <code>SentenceTransformersFinetuneEngine</code>, validating against unseen query-doc pairs.",
          "📊 <strong>Evaluation at Two Levels:</strong> 1️⃣ LlamaIndex-style top-K retrieval with hit rate scoring. 2️⃣ Deep metric evaluation with MAP and NDCG using <code>InformationRetrievalEvaluator</code> from <code>sentence_transformers</code>.",
          "🧠 <strong>Results:</strong> The fine-tuned model showed significantly improved semantic hit rates, especially on edge-case FAQs referencing multi-page documents or specialized acronyms. This wasn't just a tuning task , it was about pushing pre-trained embeddings to understand context within structured domains.",
          "#AI #LLM #NLP #EmbeddingModels #InformationRetrieval #LlamaIndex #SentenceTransformers #SemanticSearch #KnowledgeGraph #Finetuning #OpenSourceAI #Python"
        ],
        "images": [],
        "link": [
          { "label": "View on GitHub →", "href": "https://github.com/Vishnu-add/Finetuning-Embedding-Models" }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "knowledge-graph",
        "tag": "genai",
        "tagLabel": "Knowledge graphs",
        "title": "🕸️ Contextual Knowledge Graph Extraction &amp; Visualization",
        "desc": "💡 Transforms unstructured text into meaningful, interactive knowledge graphs using LLMs, identifying domain-relevant concepts and revealing relationships to bring structure and insight to raw textual data.",
        "detail": [
          "This project transforms unstructured text into meaningful, interactive knowledge graphs using LLMs.",
          "💡 It identifies domain-relevant concepts and reveals relationships, helping bring structure and insight to raw textual data. {{img:hero}}",
          "🔧 Built with Python, it leverages a powerful stack: Pandas , for structured data handling and preprocessing. 💠 LangChain , to split and manage unstructured text into manageable chunks for LLM processing. 💠 Ollama + LLaMA 3 , a local LLM setup for extracting terms and relationships with privacy and control. 💠 NetworkX , for building and analyzing the underlying graph structure. 💠 PyVis , for rendering interactive, browser-based graph visualizations.",
          "<strong>Key Highlights:</strong><ul style=\"margin:8px 0 0 20px; padding:0;\"><li>1️⃣ LLM-Powered Ontology Extraction: 💠 A custom graphPrompt pipeline processes text chunk by chunk, extracting key terms and their relationships using a language model flexible across domains like research, law, healthcare, etc.</li><li>2️⃣ Contextual Proximity Mapping: 💠 Goes beyond obvious term links. It maps how contextually close terms are, combining LLM-extracted relationships with proximity-based semantic neighborhoods to uncover deeper insights.</li><li>3️⃣ Graph Construction with Community Detection: 💠 NetworkX is used to structure the relationships as an undirected graph, followed by community detection and dynamic color encoding, helping uncover clusters of related concepts in the knowledge space.</li><li>4️⃣ Interactive HTML Visualization: 💠 The final graph is rendered using PyVis, delivering an intuitive, browser-based visualization where nodes can be explored interactively with hover-based tooltips and clustering behavior.</li><li>5️⃣ Modular &amp; Scalable Architecture: 💠 Built to be easily extended , models, parsing logic, relationship scoring, or visual styles can be swapped in and out for experimentation or domain-specific needs.</li><li>6️⃣ Multi-Layered Output Generation: 💠 Outputs include: a CSV of extracted concepts and relationships, chunk-wise insight summaries, and a full interactive HTML graph for deep exploration.</li></ul>",
          "#KnowledgeGraph #LLM #GraphVisualization #AIApplications #OpenAI #NetworkScience #DataExploration #Python #NLP #ProjectShowcase"
        ],
        "images": [
          { "id": "hero", "src": "media/images/knowledge_GRAPH.png", "caption": "Interactive knowledge graph visualization" }
        ],
        "link": [
          { "label": "View on GitHub →", "href": "https://github.com/Vishnu-add/Knowledge_graph_using_llms" }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "medextract",
        "tag": "nlp",
        "tagLabel": "NLP",
        "title": "🩺 MedExtract – Training a Medical NER Model with spaCy",
        "desc": "💡 MedExtract is a project to train a custom Named Entity Recognition (NER) model for medical text using spaCy and transformer models. It focuses on identifying terms like diseases in clinical data.",
        "detail": [
          "MedExtract is a project to train a custom Named Entity Recognition (NER) model for medical text using spaCy and transformer models. It focuses on identifying terms like diseases in clinical data.",
          "<strong>Key Highlights:</strong><ul style=\"margin:8px 0 0 20px; padding:0;\"><li>1️⃣ Data Preparation: 💠 Processed .tsv files with BIO tags and converted them into entity spans using character offsets. 💠 Mapped labels like B_Disease and I_Disease to help the model recognize medical terms.</li><li>2️⃣ spaCy Format Conversion: 💠 Converted the data into spaCy's DocBin format using char_span() with proper alignment to avoid span errors.</li><li>3️⃣ Model Training: 💠 Used roberta-base with spacy-transformers for training. 💠 Defined the pipeline in config.cfg with transformer and ner components. 💠 Trained the model on GPU with over 20,000 steps.</li><li>4️⃣ Evaluation: 💠 Evaluated the model on a validation set and real medical abstracts. 💠 Visualized predictions using displacy.</li><li>5️⃣ Model Output and Usage: 💠 The trained model is saved in the model-best folder and can be used in other spaCy pipelines. 💠 The project is modular, so components like the model or tokenizer can be easily replaced.</li></ul> {{img:hero}}",
          "#NER #spaCy #Transformers #MedicalAI #NLP"
        ],
        "images": [
          { "id": "hero", "src": "media/images/med_ner.png", "caption": "Model predictions on medical text" }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "docuchat",
        "tag": "rag",
        "tagLabel": "RAG",
        "title": "📄 DocuChat AI , RAG",
        "desc": "💡 A lightweight, responsive Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) app built using open-source LLMs and efficient vector retrieval for real-time document interaction.",
        "detail": [
          "This project delivers a lightweight, responsive Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) application built using open-source LLMs and efficient vector retrieval for real-time document interaction. {{img:hero}}",
          "🔧 Built With: LLM , LaMini-T5 (738M) from MBZUAI via HuggingFace Pipelines. 💠 Embeddings , all-MiniLM-L6-v2 from SentenceTransformers. 💠 Vector Store , ChromaDB. 💠 Frontend , Streamlit for PDF preview and chat interface.",
          "<strong>Key Highlights:</strong><ul style=\"margin:8px 0 0 20px; padding:0;\"><li>1️⃣ RAG Pipeline Integration: 💠 Integrated LangChain's RetrievalQA chain with a HuggingFacePipeline-backed LLM. Uses a retriever over ChromaDB to fetch semantically relevant chunks from the uploaded PDF, enabling grounded responses.</li><li>2️⃣ Efficient Document Processing: 💠 Uses PDFMinerLoader to load documents and RecursiveCharacterTextSplitter to chunk them. Embeddings are generated on the fly and stored in Chroma for fast vector search.</li><li>3️⃣ HuggingFacePipeline for LLM Invocation: 💠 A pre-loaded pipeline using LaMini-T5 is wrapped into a LangChain-compatible LLM using HuggingFacePipeline. This avoids custom tokenizer and generation logic, keeping the implementation clean and efficient.</li><li>4️⃣ CPU-Optimized Deployment: 💠 Despite using a 738M parameter model, the system runs smoothly on CPU by leveraging efficient caching and memory use , no GPU dependency.</li><li>5️⃣ Interactive PDF Preview &amp; Chat: 💠 Built-in PDF preview alongside the chat window. Once the document is embedded, users can ask questions in real time.</li><li>6️⃣ Session-Based Chat History: 💠 Maintains chat history, allowing multi-turn conversation with contextual memory. Includes an option to clear chat for new interactions.</li><li>7️⃣ Persistent Vector Storage: 💠 Embeddings are stored in a persisted ChromaDB directory to avoid recomputation on repeated document interactions.</li></ul>",
          "#RAG #LangChain #HuggingFace #LLMs #Embeddings #ChromaDB #Streamlit #Python #DocumentAI #OpenSource #GenerativeAI #PDFChatbot #ProjectShowcase"
        ],
        "images": [
          { "id": "hero", "src": "media/images/docu_chat.png", "caption": "DocuChat AI , PDF chat interface" }
        ],
        "link": [
          { "label": "View on GitHub →", "href": "https://github.com/Vishnu-add/Chat_with_your_pdf" }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "indian-food-classification-showcase",
        "tag": "vision",
        "tagLabel": "Computer vision",
        "title": "🍛 Image Classification for Indian Food Recognition",
        "desc": "💡 Identifies various types of Indian food from images using a fine-tuned Vision Transformer (ViT), built with Python, Hugging Face Transformers, PyTorch, and torchvision, from data preprocessing through model training and deployment.",
        "detail": [
          "This project aims to accurately identify various types of Indian food from images using deep learning techniques, specifically leveraging the Vision Transformer (ViT) model.",
          "💡 Image Classification for Indian Food Recognition helps users automatically categorize Indian food items by analyzing their images. This project utilizes the power of computer vision and deep learning to deliver precise food identification. {{img:sample}}",
          "🔧 Built with Python and utilizing libraries such as Hugging Face Transformers, PyTorch, and torchvision, this project involves several key steps from data preprocessing to model training and deployment.",
          "<strong>Key Highlights:</strong><ul style=\"margin:8px 0 0 20px; padding:0;\"><li>1️⃣ Data Collection: 💠 Utilized a custom dataset of Indian food images, containing multiple classes representing different types of Indian dishes. The dataset was uploaded to Hugging Face's dataset hub for easy access and management.</li><li>2️⃣ Data Preprocessing: 💠 Image Augmentation , applied transformations such as random resizing, horizontal flipping, resizing, and normalization to enhance the dataset and ensure images are in the correct format for the model. 💠 Feature Extraction , used ViTFeatureExtractor to preprocess the images, making them compatible with the Vision Transformer model.</li><li>3️⃣ Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA): 💠 Analyzed the distribution of images across different food categories to ensure a balanced dataset. 💠 Visualized sample images from each category to understand the variations within the data.</li><li>4️⃣ Model Training: 💠 Fine-Tuned Vision Transformer (ViT) , adapted the ViT model to classify Indian food images by adjusting it to the specific dataset. 💠 Training Configuration , set parameters such as batch size, learning rate, and number of epochs to optimize model performance. 💠 Utilized Hugging Face's Trainer API , managed the training and evaluation process efficiently, incorporating features like mixed precision training (fp16) and evaluation metrics tracking.</li><li>5️⃣ Model Evaluation: 💠 Evaluated the model using metrics such as accuracy to measure its performance on the validation set. 💠 Monitored training and validation losses to ensure the model is learning effectively without overfitting. {{img:scores}}</li><li>6️⃣ Model Deployment: 💠 Saved the trained model for future inference tasks. 💠 Integrated the model into a user-friendly interface where users can upload images and receive food classification results in real-time.</li></ul>",
          "#ImageClassification #DeepLearning #ComputerVision #Python #HuggingFace #ViT #FoodRecognition #MachineLearning #ProjectShowcase"
        ],
        "images": [
          { "id": "sample", "src": "media/images/Indian_food_classification/Fried Rice.png", "caption": "Sample prediction , Fried Rice" },
          { "id": "scores", "src": "media/images/Indian_food_classification/scores.png", "caption": "Model evaluation scores" }
        ],
        "link": [
          { "label": "View on GitHub →", "href": "https://github.com/Vishnu-add/Image-Classification-for-Food-Recognition" }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "face-mask-detector-showcase",
        "tag": "vision",
        "tagLabel": "Computer vision",
        "title": "😷 Real-Time Face Mask Detector",
        "desc": "💡 Classifies whether individuals in a live video stream are wearing face masks, combining TensorFlow, OpenCV, and Gradio to deliver accurate and efficient mask detection.",
        "detail": [
          "💡 Real-Time Face Mask Detector enables users to classify whether individuals in a live video stream are wearing face masks. This project combines TensorFlow, OpenCV, and Gradio to deliver accurate and efficient mask detection.",
          "🔧 Built with Python and utilizing TensorFlow, OpenCV, and Gradio, this project involves several key steps from data preprocessing to deployment as a web application.",
          "<strong>Key Highlights:</strong><ul style=\"margin:8px 0 0 20px; padding:0;\"><li>1️⃣ Face Detection: 💠 Leveraged a pre-trained MobileNetV2 model for accurate and efficient face detection in real-time.</li><li>2️⃣ Mask Detection: 💠 Trained a custom model to classify faces as either wearing a mask or not wearing a mask, ensuring high accuracy in various scenarios.</li><li>3️⃣ Integration with Gradio: 💠 Developed a seamless interface using Gradio for webcam-based deployment, allowing users to monitor and detect mask usage through their browser.</li><li>4️⃣ Live Video Stream Processing: 💠 Employed OpenCV for handling real-time video streams, enabling the system to process and classify faces continuously.</li><li>5️⃣ Model Inference: 💠 Batched predictions for multiple faces detected in a frame, enhancing the efficiency of mask detection.</li><li>6️⃣ User-Friendly Interface: 💠 Created an interactive Gradio interface where users can see real-time results of mask detection on their webcam feed.</li></ul>",
          "#MachineLearning #ComputerVision #Python #TensorFlow #OpenCV #Gradio #FaceMaskDetection #ProjectShowcase"
        ],
        "images": [],
        "videos": ["media/images/Mask_detector.mp4"],
        "link": [
          { "label": "View on GitHub →", "href": "https://github.com/Vishnu-add/Real_TimeFace_Mask_Detector" }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "sentiment-analysis-showcase",
        "tag": "nlp",
        "tagLabel": "NLP",
        "title": "🐦 Sentiment Analysis of Twitter Data",
        "desc": "💡 A sentiment classification project combining NLP and Machine Learning to predict whether tweets are positive or negative, built with Python, NLTK, scikit-learn, and Flask, from data preprocessing through model training and deployment.",
        "detail": [
          "This particular project was developed to analyze and understand the sentiment behind tweets.",
          "💡 Sentiment Analysis of Twitter Data allows users to classify the sentiment of tweets as either positive or negative. This project combines the power of Natural Language Processing (NLP) and Machine Learning to deliver accurate sentiment predictions.",
          "🔧 Built with Python and leveraging libraries such as NLTK, scikit-learn, and Flask, this project involves several key steps from data preprocessing to model training and deployment as a web application.",
          "<strong>Key Highlights:</strong><ul style=\"margin:8px 0 0 20px; padding:0;\"><li>1️⃣ Data Collection: 💠 Utilized the Sentiment140 dataset from Kaggle, which contains 1.6 million tweets labeled as positive or negative. This large dataset provides a robust foundation for training an effective sentiment analysis model.</li><li>2️⃣ Text Preprocessing: 💠 Cleaning , removed Twitter handles, URLs, special characters, and numbers from the tweets to reduce noise. 💠 Lowercasing , converted all text to lowercase to ensure uniformity. 💠 Tokenization , split the text into individual words (tokens). 💠 Stemming , applied Porter Stemmer to reduce words to their root form, e.g., \"running\" to \"run.\" 💠 Stopwords Removal , removed common words that do not contribute to sentiment, such as \"and,\" \"the,\" etc.</li><li>3️⃣ Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA): 💠 Generated word clouds to visualize the most frequent words in positive and negative tweets, helping to understand the data distribution and key terms associated with each sentiment. {{img:wordcloud}}</li><li>4️⃣ Feature Extraction: 💠 Used TfidfVectorizer to convert the cleaned text into numerical vectors. TF-IDF (Term Frequency-Inverse Document Frequency) is a statistical measure used to evaluate the importance of a word in a document relative to a collection of documents.</li><li>5️⃣ Model Training: 💠 Split the data into training and testing sets (80% training, 20% testing). 💠 Trained a Logistic Regression model to predict the sentiment of tweets. 💠 The model was evaluated using metrics such as accuracy, F1 score, and recall, achieving impressive performance on both the training and testing datasets.</li><li>6️⃣ Model Evaluation: 💠 Training Data , achieved an accuracy of 99.68%, indicating the model's effectiveness in learning from the training data. 💠 Testing Data , achieved an accuracy of 75.63%, demonstrating the model's generalization ability to unseen data. 💠 Saved the trained model using pickle for future use in the web application. {{img:results}}</li><li>7️⃣ Flask Web Application: 💠 Developed a web interface where users can input a tweet and receive a sentiment prediction. 💠 The web application, built using Flask, integrates the trained model for real-time sentiment analysis, offering a user-friendly experience.</li></ul>",
          "#SentimentAnalysis #MachineLearning #NLP #Python #Flask #DataScience #TwitterData #ProjectShowcase"
        ],
        "images": [
          { "id": "wordcloud", "src": "media/images/Sentiment_analysis/image.png", "caption": "Word cloud of frequent tweet terms" },
          { "id": "results", "src": "media/images/Sentiment_analysis/image-1.png", "caption": "Model training vs. testing accuracy" }
        ],
        "link": [
          { "label": "View on GitHub →", "href": "https://github.com/Vishnu-add/Sentiment-Analysis-of-Social-Media-Data" }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "textreaderaudiobook",
        "tag": "python",
        "tagLabel": "Python",
        "title": "🎧 Text_reader_and_Audio_Book",
        "desc": "A comprehensive text-to-audio conversion project! Developed early in my learning journey, this Python command-line app converts PDF, TXT, and DOCX files into speech or MP3 format. Its functionality has since been replaced by browser updates, but it remains a milestone in my growth as a programmer.",
        "detail": [
          "🎧 Developed long back to assist in my learning journey, Text_reader_and_Audio_Book is a Python project designed to facilitate the conversion of text content from PDF, TXT, and DOCX files into speech or MP3 format. This project was instrumental in my growth and exploration in the field of programming, and although browser updates have replaced its functionality, I am sharing it to showcase the project.",
          "🛠️ This command-line application leverages powerful libraries like Pyttsx3, PyPDF2, and docx2txt for efficient file handling and text-to-speech conversion.",
          "<strong>Key highlights:</strong><ul style=\"margin:8px 0 0 20px; padding:0;\"><li>1️⃣ Multi-format support , convert PDF, TXT, and DOCX files into speech or MP3 format effortlessly.</li><li>2️⃣ Text-to-speech conversion , access text content in an auditory format, catering to visually impaired individuals and auditory learners.</li><li>3️⃣ Selective conversion , choose to convert the entire document or specific pages according to your preferences.</li><li>4️⃣ Voice selection , customize your listening experience by selecting from a variety of voices for text narration.</li><li>5️⃣ Customization options , adjust reading speed to your liking for a comfortable listening experience.</li></ul>",
          "🚀 Text_reader_and_Audio_Book remains a valuable project, especially for those seeking auditory access to textual content. It serves as a foundation for future innovations in assistive technology and personal productivity tools.",
          "#TextToAudio #Python #Accessibility #Productivity #Text_reader_and_Audio_Book"
        ],
        "images": [],
        "videos": ["media/images/Text_reader_and_audio_book.mp4"],
        "link": [
          { "label": "View on GitHub →", "href": "https://github.com/Vishnu-add/Text_reader_and_Audio_Book" }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "virtualmouse",
        "tag": "vision",
        "tagLabel": "Vision",
        "title": "🖱️ Virtual Mouse",
        "desc": "The first project I ever built, and the one that got me hooked on this field. Controls the computer cursor through hand gestures, using MediaPipe hand tracking over a live webcam feed to let you operate your machine from across the room.",
        "detail": [
          "This was my first project, built a while back, and it's the one that sparked my interest in this whole field. I used it to operate my computer from a distance within my room, just by moving my hand in front of the webcam.",
          "💡 Virtual Mouse lets you control your computer cursor through hand gestures.",
          "🔧 Built with Python and OpenCV, it's a real-time computer vision application that leverages MediaPipe's Hand Tracking solution to detect hand landmarks from the webcam feed. By analyzing the movement of specific landmarks like the index finger and thumb, users can effortlessly maneuver the cursor and perform actions like clicking.",
          "<strong>Key highlights:</strong><ul style=\"margin:8px 0 0 20px; padding:0;\"><li>1️⃣ Hand gesture detection , real-time hand movement tracking using the MediaPipe library.</li><li>2️⃣ Cursor movement , mapping hand landmarks to screen coordinates for seamless cursor control.</li><li>3️⃣ Click actions , recognizing gestures for mouse click simulation, enhancing interaction efficiency.</li><li>4️⃣ Responsive interface , smooth and intuitive cursor control for enhanced productivity and comfort.</li></ul>"
        ],
        "images": [],
        "videos": ["media/images/Virtual Mouse Project.mp4"],
        "link": [
          { "label": "View on GitHub →", "href": "https://github.com/Vishnu-add/VirtualMouse" }
        ]
      }
    ]
